 "note": "Councils read ONCE BY HAND in a web browser (Adam's own Chrome, on his ruling of 2026-11-25) because this project's weekly reader cannot read the nation's site: it refuses the reader, its robots.txt answers with a server error, its certificate does not cover the address the Bureau lists, or the page draws its council only in a browser. scripts/tribal_council_scraper.py never fetches these pages; it copies each record into data/tribal-councils.json with readBy \"browser\", and the card says the names were read by hand and on which date. Each record is what the page printed that day, checked by the scraper's own tests (seat count, names, offices). A record leaves by the page becoming readable to the weekly reader or by a new read.",
